    "lawCode": "Amd §211-d, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S10615\n\nSPONSOR: LIU\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to contracts for excel-\nlence in a city school district in a city having a population of one\nmillion or more inhabitants\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nTo provide additional time for the implementation of class size\nreduction requirements in the city school district of the city of New\nYork.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends the contracts for excellence statute as it relates to\nNew York City to extend the deadline by 2 additional years for New York\nCity to develop a class size reduction plan to reduce class sizes.\n\nSection 2 - Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation amends class size reduction requirements in the city\nschool district of the city of New York by extending the deadline for\nfull compliance by 2 years.  The extended legal timeline authorized by\nthis act supports continued planning and coordination consistent with\nexisting statutory requirements and broader educational objectives.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act takes effect on July 1st, 2026\n",
